                {"code": "AGR.1", "name": "Alley Cropping Light Competition", "formula": "L_reduction = (1 − exp(−k × LAI × (1 − d/H))) × 100", "variables": "k = light extinction coeff (0.4-0.6)\nLAI = tree leaf area index\nd = distance from tree row (m)\nH = tree height (m)", "purpose": "Estimate light reduction at crop level as function of distance from tree row. Design alley width to minimize competition.", "example": "Tree H=8m, LAI=3, k=0.5. At d=4m: L = (1−exp(−0.5×3×0.5))×100 = 53% light reduction. Too much — widen alley.", "pitfall": "Light varies by tree species + pruning. Deciduous trees lose leaves in winter (light for winter crop).", "decision": "Minimum alley width = 1× tree height for acceptable light (>50%).", "notes": "Jackson & Wallace (1999). Pruning reduces LAI and competition.", "name_ar": "منافسة الضوء في الزراعة البينية", "purpose_ar": "تقدير تقليل الضوء عند مستوى المحصول حسب المسافة من شجرة.", "variables_ar": "k = معامل انقراض الضوء\nLAI = مؤشر مساحة الأوراق"},
